---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="How Louis Gimeno moved from computer science and QA into cloud engineering, DevOps, and cloud support engineering."
  path="/about/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>From software quality to cloud platform engineering</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        My career has moved step by step toward cloud platform work, and each step built a skill I use today.
      </p>

      <h2>Education and QA foundations</h2>
      <p>
        I studied Computer Science at Adamson University and graduated Magna Cum Laude. My first professional role was a QA
        internship at Stratpoint Technologies, where I wrote test plans and test cases, did manual and automated testing, and
        worked in an Agile team. That work taught me to investigate systematically and to validate a result before calling it
        done.
      </p>

      <h2>Cloud engineering and DevOps</h2>
      <p>
        I then worked as a Cloud Engineer and later a DevOps Engineer at Stratpoint. The work included monitoring and
        operating AWS and Azure resources, working with CI/CD pipelines in Jenkins and GitLab, using Terraform and
        CloudFormation, and working with Docker and Kubernetes.
      </p>

      <h2>Cloud L2 support and complex troubleshooting</h2>
      <p>
        At HCLSoftware I work as a Cloud L2 Support Engineer on HCL Workload Automation and UnO, across SaaS and on-premises
        environments. The role centers on investigating complex product, application, integration, and infrastructure issues,
        analyzing logs to find likely root causes, reproducing problems, and working with development and DevOps teams.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>I investigate from evidence: logs, events, and monitoring data.</li>
        <li>I document findings and resolutions so other engineers can act on them.</li>
        <li>I collaborate with development, DevOps, and engineering teams, and communicate technical recommendations clearly.</li>
        <li>I am careful to separate what I investigated, recommended, and implemented.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where I am heading</h2>
      <p>
        I am interested in cloud platforms, Kubernetes, automation, and reliability. I am building public projects to show that
        work openly: <a href={href('/projects/')}>see what is planned</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={href('/experience/')}>View experience</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href={href('/contact/')}>Contact me</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
